+# Batch 65 authoring evidence
+
+## Scope, plan, and design
+
+- Owned pair: `qftx-gaga-local-coherent-acyclicity` / `qftx-gaga-local-coherent-acyclicity-examples`.
+- No pair-specific design section was found. The exact plan-spec theorem contract governs; no design/plan conflict was found. The authored scope remains local coherent acyclicity on every nonempty coordinate polydisc inside one sufficiently small resolution polydisc, plus scalar Dolbeault computation. It asserts no global Stein generation, Cartan A/B, or global free resolution.
+- The plan's proof route is preserved: scalar Dolbeault acyclicity, partial finite free resolution, dimension shift, and ordinary cohomological dimension at most `2N`. Three local A-page supports were added so the dimension bound does not rely on compact-support cohomology or an unproved cover assertion.
+- The initial batch inventory had no items. The populated A page now contains the Čech/derived comparison theorem (level 0), Euclidean finite-order refinement lemma (level 0), ordinary Euclidean sheaf cohomological-dimension lemma (level 1), and the main theorem (level 3). The B page contains both quotient examples (level 4). Initial plan levels were 2/3 for the main/example items; the actual inspected batch-63 Oka carrier is level 2, and the new in-batch supports give the recomputed levels 3/4. The page-level prerequisite remains batch 63, level 1.
+
+## Items and arguments
+
+| Item | Claim and conventions | Dependencies / disposition |
+|---|---|---|
+| `thm-qftx-gaga-metric-cech-derived-comparison` | Under full AC, for any metric space and abelian sheaf, refinement-limit ordered Čech cohomology is naturally the right-derived global-sections cohomology. Ordinary sheaf cohomology only. | `def-axiom-of-choice`, metric/paracompactness and shrinking, sheaf/Čech definitions, enough injectives, stalkwise exactness, flasque/Leray, delta-functor uniqueness and long exact sequence. The local proof gives the cochain-lifting and effacement arguments. Level 0. |
+| `lem-qftx-gaga-euclidean-finite-order-refinement` | Under full AC, every open cover of a nonempty open `Omega subset R^m` has a locally finite open refinement of pointwise order at most `m+1`. | `def-axiom-of-choice`, `def-metric-space`. The proof constructs an adaptive dyadic cube complex and uses vertex stars. Level 0. |
+| `lem-qftx-gaga-euclidean-sheaf-cohomological-dimension` | For every abelian sheaf on a Euclidean open subset of `R^m`, ordinary derived cohomology vanishes in degrees `q>m`. | AC, sheaf cohomology and ordered Čech definitions, the preceding two local results. Explicitly not a compact-support statement. Level 1. |
+| `thm-qftx-gaga-local-coherent-acyclicity` | For coherent analytic `F` near `x in C^N`, a coordinate polydisc `W` has `H^q(D,F|D)=0` for every nonempty coordinate polydisc `D subset W` and `q>0`; scalar cohomology is computed by the smooth Dolbeault complex. A partial resolution of length `2N+1` is used locally. | Plan suppliers: AC; Oka local resolution/coherence; Dolbeault lemma and polydisc vanishing; smooth-module acyclicity; acyclic resolution; injectives/derived sections; stalkwise exactness; sheaf-cohomology long exact sequence; local ordinary dimension bound. Level 3. **Conditional consuming proof is complete, but readiness is escalated** because the current Oka readiness record and a transitive bounded-degree-relations helper record are hash-stale. |
+| `ex-qftx-gaga-point-quotient-coherent-acyclicity` | On a supplied `W`, `O/(z_1,...,z_N)` is the skyscraper sheaf `i_* C` at the origin; `H^0=C` and positive ordinary cohomology vanishes. | AC, coherent-module/Oka closure, convergent power series, skyscraper definition, stalkwise isomorphism, main theorem. Level 4. Its carrier explicitly records the same unresolved Oka readiness input. |
+| `ex-qftx-gaga-hyperplane-quotient-coherent-acyclicity` | On a supplied `W`, `O/(z_1)` is `i_* O_H` for `H={z_1=0}`; global sections are holomorphic functions on `H`, with positive ordinary cohomology zero. | AC, coherent-module/Oka closure, direct-image definition and sheaf property, stalkwise isomorphism, convergent power-series expansion and coefficient uniqueness, main theorem. Level 4. Its carrier explicitly records the same unresolved Oka readiness input. |
+
+## Cross-batch prerequisite inspection
+
+The current `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-oka-coherence` statement and complete proof were reread after its batch-63 inventory appeared. Its actual interface says that, under AC, every coherent module on a finite-dimensional complex manifold has a chart neighborhood with a partial finite-rank free resolution of each prescribed finite length, exact at the module and all free terms except the leftmost; it also supplies coherent-kernel/cokernel/extension closure. The interface and proof match the conditional use in the main theorem and both examples. The current batch-63 manifest now lists all five items. `def-qftx-analytic-coherent-module` has an unchanged current ready record. The Oka theorem has an existing `ready` record whose hash is stale; its transitive `lem-qftx-gaga-analytic-bounded-degree-relations` helper also has a stale `ready` record. This is a fresh current readiness gap. The Oka carrier's draft status and `verification.precheck: pending` are not treated as gaps by themselves. The consuming proofs therefore remain conditional and are escalated rather than marked ready.
+
+The exact cross-batch rows are in `advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-65.cross-batch-dependencies.json`: the A page to batch-63's A page remains `open` because Oka and a transitive helper have stale readiness; each consumer-to-Oka edge is `open`; each consumer-to-coherent-definition edge is `verified` as a scoped interface/current-record check, not independent proof approval. Owner action proposed: refresh the existing Step 1 records for `thm-qftx-gaga-analytic-oka-coherence` and `lem-qftx-gaga-analytic-bounded-degree-relations` on batch 63's `qftx-gaga-analytic-coherence` A page. Those current carriers match the interface; no new supplier result is proposed. Affected claims are the main theorem and both quotient examples. No batch-63 item or page was edited.
+
+## Sources read and result disposition
+
+- Demailly, *Analytic Methods in Algebraic Geometry*, official full PDF: <https://www-fourier.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/~demailly/manuscripts/agbook.pdf>, Chapter IX §4.B, Proposition 4.1, equation (4.3), Lemma 4.4 and complete proof, printed pp. 419–421. A prior browser open timed out; the corrected official Grenoble host returned the 455-page full PDF, which was inspected at the cited range. The source's scalar vanishing, local partial resolution, and dimension shift are inline in the main theorem; its dimension estimate is made explicit in the local Euclidean cohomological-dimension lemma. For the examples, the source supports only application of the coherent-vanishing theorem; the quotient/stalk identifications are proved locally.
+- Wehler, *Stein Manifolds*, official full lecture notes: <https://www.math.lmu.de/~wehler/20190530_Stein_Manifolds_script.pdf>, §5.2, Proposition 5.9, Theorem 5.14 and Corollary 5.15, complete proofs, printed pp. 171–180. These independently support the scalar and coherent local vanishing route. The inspected proof assumes a full finite free resolution and relatively compact polydiscs, so those hypotheses are not imported into the broader every-subpolydisc claim.
+- Demailly, “Sheaf cohomology and the De Rham-Weil isomorphism theorem,” full text: <https://www-fourier.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/~demailly/analytic_geometry_2019/sheaves_cech_cohomology.pdf>, §1.A–1.C, PDF pp. 1–5. The refinement-limit definition, paracompact cochain-lifting argument and Leray comparison proof are absorbed into `thm-qftx-gaga-metric-cech-derived-comparison`.
+- Agol, *Complex Analysis and Riemann Surfaces*, full course notes: <https://math.berkeley.edu/~ianagol/complexri.pdf>, §6, Theorem 6.5, PDF p. 29. The finite-cover dimension argument is included in the Euclidean refinement and ordinary cohomological-dimension lemmas; the full refinement and derived-comparison proofs are supplied locally.
+
+The per-page `coverage.json` entries record each source's locator, supported item, source-read range, limitations, and `included`/`inline` disposition. No source is dropped, so no alternative proof is being used to waive coverage.
+
